From ba810b5faab91daac4046de12e20bd1895000eed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wainohito <wainohito@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:43:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] platform: compose input method text inline

Qt windows did not handle B_INPUT_METHOD_EVENT, so input methods such
as Mozc fell back to the input_server bottom-line window.

Add QHaikuInputContext, a QPlatformInputContext that turns the input
method events into QInputMethodEvents (clauses underlined, the clause
being converted highlighted, commit), answers location requests with
the cursor rectangle, and ends the composition when Qt resets it or
the focus moves. The surface view is marked B_INPUT_METHOD_AWARE, and
given the focus, while the focused object accepts input methods, so
other widgets keep the bottom-line window.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5

How this was tested: not built yet; ported from the Qt 6 change, which
was tested with FeatherPad.

Signed-off-by: wainohito <wainohito@gmail.com>
